judge.reasoning:
Both patches make an unset baseURL resolve to https://example.org/, so both address the issue. B is the better fix.

Correctness: B registers the default in `applyDefaultConfig` through `SetDefaults`. This is the same mechanism Hugo uses for other default settings, so the value shows up consistently, including in `hugo config` output. Because `SetDefaults` only fills keys that are absent, a user who explicitly sets `baseURL = ""` keeps an empty base URL. B's TestAlias update relies on exactly that for the relativeURLs case. A instead patches `CompileConfig` to replace any empty string with example.org. That makes an explicit empty baseURL impossible, which is why A has to rewrite many tests to use `baseURL = "/"`. It is also a post-hoc fix-up inside compilation rather than a real default. B additionally updates `docs/data/docs.yaml` so the documented default matches the new behaviour.

Tests: B adds integration tests covering:
- the default value itself, plus its effect on `absURL` and `.Permalink`;
- an explicit override;
- multihost per-language baseURLs still taking precedence over the default;
- testscripts for `hugo config` output and for `hugo server` replacing the default with localhost.
B also updates the existing expectations to the new absolute URLs, which documents the real behaviour change. A adds a smaller test (default, override, and "/"). Its other test edits mostly pin `baseURL = "/"` to preserve the old output, which hides the effect of the change rather than exercising it.

Scope and craft: A carries a large amount of unrelated reformatting, splitting every `AssertFileContent("path",` call across lines in several test files. That churn obscures the real change. B's diff is focused and follows existing conventions.

